---
const stats = [
  ['CFA', 'Charterholder-designed'],
  ['~20 yrs', 'In global markets'],
]
---
<section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
    <span class="flex items-center justify-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-black/50 mb-5">
      <span class="h-px w-6 bg-[#FFBD40]"></span>
      Why The Money Wit
    </span>
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl text-black">Designed by a CFA Charterholder with almost 20 years in global markets.</h2>
    <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-black/60">
      The Money Wit is an expert financial education ecosystem for individuals and organisations. This tool applies the same discipline used in professional markets to personal finances which is why it is a planning framework rather than a budget template.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {stats.map(([big, small]) => (
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-black/10 p-6">
          <div class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-[#FFBD40]">{big}</div>
          <div class="mt-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-black/40">{small}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
